      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your critique highlights a significant gap between economic theory and real-world evidence; most OECD studies, including those from Cambridge University, consistently show little to no adverse impact on capital flight or investment when such taxes are implemented. Countries that have tried inherited wealth taxes, such as Queensland, Australia, and Norway, demonstrate that nuanced design and strong enforcement reliably prevent massive capital outfoxes while effectively raising necessary revenue. Consequently, the consensus among experienced economists is that these tools are viable for redistribution, provided they are structured to avoid chilling investment.",
